		(components/display) with the BL616CL controller backends. Board
		code defines the bus, the panel module and its control pins, and
		registers the display as a NuttX LCD device.

if BL616CL_DISPLAY

menuconfig BL616CL_DBI
	bool "DBI controller bus"
	default y
	---help---
		Display bus on the DBI controller: MIPI DBI type B (8080, 8 data
		lines), type C 3-wire and 4-wire, and QSPI panels. Commands and
		parameters are written to the FIFO by the CPU.

if BL616CL_DBI

config BL616CL_DBI_CLK_MODE
	int "Clock polarity and phase of the serial interfaces"
	default 1
	range 0 3
	---help---
		DBI_CLOCK_MODE_0..3 of the type C and QSPI interfaces, common to
		all endpoints of the bus. The SDK default is 1.

menuconfig BL616CL_DBI_DMA
	bool "Send pixels with DMA0"
	default y
	depends on BL616CL_DMA0
	---help---
		DMA0 feeds the pixels to the DBI FIFO and the draw ends with the
		DBI transfer-complete interrupt. Without it the CPU writes the
		pixels to the FIFO, which is meant for bring-up and debugging.
		The channel is set in "DMA0 channel assignment".

if BL616CL_DBI_DMA

config BL616CL_DBI_DMA_LLI_COUNT
	int "DMA0 LLI nodes per draw"
	default 40
	range 1 255
	---help---
		Largest draw, in DMA0 LLI nodes of 16256 bytes: 40 nodes carry
		650240 bytes, two 320x480 RGB565 frames. A draw takes its nodes
		from BL616CL_DMA0_LLI_NODES while it runs; the build fails if that
		pool holds fewer than this count minus one.

endif # BL616CL_DBI_DMA

endif # BL616CL_DBI

menuconfig BL616CL_DISPLAY_SPI
	bool "SPI controller bus"
	default n
	depends on !BL616CL_SPI0 || !BL616CL_SPI1
	---help---
		Display bus on an SPI controller: MIPI DBI type C 4-wire (SCK,
		MOSI, DC on a GPIO) with RGB565 and XRGB8888 pixels. Commands and
		parameters are sent by polling. The controller belongs to the
		display and cannot also be a NuttX SPI bus, so one of SPI0 and
		SPI1 must be free.

if BL616CL_DISPLAY_SPI

choice
	prompt "SPI controller"
	default BL616CL_DISPLAY_SPI_PORT0

config BL616CL_DISPLAY_SPI_PORT0
	bool "SPI0"
	depends on !BL616CL_SPI0

